to the tier-ownership matrix even though the runner executes it). Both are recorded in the W1 records and re-carried here; registering them as register rows would change the frozen plan body and force a rebind of in-flight waves' trios.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W5 owner (artifact provenance and determinism)") (rationale . "The gate receives the content digest as a caller-supplied --content-digest value and only checks that the record agrees with what it was handed, so the chain 'recompute the digest from the diff' lives outside the gate that enforces it - the F1 shape one level up. This wave narrows the exposure by shipping the tool that computes the digest (gsd-evidence-bind digest/verify/bind) and by binding the wave's own records to its recomputed value (base 69647f1c pinned at review time), but making the gate itself recompute is W5's subject, as recorded in W1.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W7 owner (blocked wave repair, bake, release)") (rationale . "record-commit-purity scans only commits that touch the evidence record directory (docs/reports/gsd-wave-evidence/), so a commit mixing only the reviews/validation record directories with a source path would not be flagged by the tool; the normative record commit always includes the evidence file, and prepare() additionally refuses at staging time, so the narrow reading is not a live hole - flagged by the round-2 review and documented rather than silently widened. Widening the scan belongs with the bake/release owner who owns the final record-commit surface.")))) (review-artifact . "docs/reports/gsd-wave-reviews/v1.00.31-w2.rktd") (status . "current") (wave . "W2") (workflows . #hasheq((command . "not run locally this wave") (detail . "The wave touches no workflow file and no script the workflows suite executes; the suites the wave's Verify block names (focused, arch, fast) plus check-deps and metrics --lint all pass at the final head, and the w